(1) N = 64: the real subring Z[theta], theta = 2 cos(2 pi / N)
  the minimal polynomial Psi_N(t) = P_(N/4)(t), degree 16, coefficients [2, 0, -64, 0, 336, 0, -672, 0, 660, 0, -352, 0, 104, 0, -16, 0, 1]
  check: Psi_N(theta) at 60 digits = 3.000e-55 (zero to the digits kept)
  the basis: 1 and 2 cos(d a) for d = 1 .. 15 (a = 2 pi / N): 16 integers per element
  the reduction of every cos(d a), d in Z_N, to the basis by the circle's symmetries alone:
    cos((N/2 - d) a) = -cos(d a), cos((N/4) a) = 0, cos((N - d) a) = cos(d a)
  the weight w = sum over d in Z_N of c_d cos(d a), c_d = sum_j f_j f_(j+d) (the autocorrelation):
    e_0 = c_0 - c_(N/2),  e_d = 2 (c_d - c_(N/2 - d)) for d = 1 .. N/4 - 1,  w = e_0 + sum_d e_d cos(d a)
  check: on 20 random phase-count vectors |e . cos - (X^2 + Y^2)| at most 3.4e-53
  the coefficients' size: |e_d| <= 2 sum_j f_j^2 <= 2 (sum_j f_j)^2 = 2 A^2, A the summed amplitude 32 x amount

(1) N = 4096: the real subring Z[theta], theta = 2 cos(2 pi / N)
  the minimal polynomial Psi_N(t) = P_(N/4)(t), degree 1024, the largest coefficient 707 bits (not printed)
  check of Psi_N(theta): not made, the cancellation at this degree needs more than 60 digits
  the basis: 1 and 2 cos(d a) for d = 1 .. 1023 (a = 2 pi / N): 1024 integers per element
  the reduction of every cos(d a), d in Z_N, to the basis by the circle's symmetries alone:
    cos((N/2 - d) a) = -cos(d a), cos((N/4) a) = 0, cos((N - d) a) = cos(d a)
  the weight w = sum over d in Z_N of c_d cos(d a), c_d = sum_j f_j f_(j+d) (the autocorrelation):
    e_0 = c_0 - c_(N/2),  e_d = 2 (c_d - c_(N/2 - d)) for d = 1 .. N/4 - 1,  w = e_0 + sum_d e_d cos(d a)
  check: on 2 random phase-count vectors |e . cos - (X^2 + Y^2)| at most 3.7e-49
  the coefficients' size: |e_d| <= 2 sum_j f_j^2 <= 2 (sum_j f_j)^2 = 2 A^2, A the summed amplitude 32 x amount

(2) the sign of an element x = sum e_d 2cos(d a) (an algebraic integer of degree 16) at N = 64
  x = 0 exactly iff every e_d = 0 (the basis is a basis); otherwise |N(x)| >= 1 over the 16 conjugates,
  each conjugate at most 2 sum_d |e_d| in size, so |x| >= (2 sum_d |e_d|)^-(15)
  A = 2^10 (sum |e_d| <= 2 A^2 = 2^21): the precision that decides the sign, 347 bits
  A = 2^20 (sum |e_d| <= 2 A^2 = 2^41): the precision that decides the sign, 647 bits
  A = 2^25 (sum |e_d| <= 2 A^2 = 2^51): the precision that decides the sign, 797 bits
  the rung: u < b_k  iff  2 W C_k - (2 u + 1) T >= 0, one element of the ring (C_k, T cumulative weights);
  the vector of its coefficients is exact (additions), equality is the zero vector, the sign as above.

(2) the sign of an element x = sum e_d 2cos(d a) (an algebraic integer of degree 1024) at N = 4096
  x = 0 exactly iff every e_d = 0 (the basis is a basis); otherwise |N(x)| >= 1 over the 1024 conjugates,
  each conjugate at most 2 sum_d |e_d| in size, so |x| >= (2 sum_d |e_d|)^-(1023)
  A = 2^10 (sum |e_d| <= 2 A^2 = 2^21): the precision that decides the sign, 23531 bits
  A = 2^20 (sum |e_d| <= 2 A^2 = 2^41): the precision that decides the sign, 43991 bits
  A = 2^25 (sum |e_d| <= 2 A^2 = 2^51): the precision that decides the sign, 54221 bits
  the rung: u < b_k  iff  2 W C_k - (2 u + 1) T >= 0, one element of the ring (C_k, T cumulative weights);
  the vector of its coefficients is exact (additions), equality is the zero vector, the sign as above.

(4) the tables at 1/256 against the exact circle, N = 64
  |C_d - 256 cos(d a)| at most 0.4868 (<= 1/2 by the rounding); C_d^2 + S_d^2 from 65448 to 65773 against 65536
  the entries at the multiples of N/4: C = 256, 0, -256, 0; S = 0, 256, 0, -256 (exact)
  the entry at N/8 (45 degrees): C = 181 against 128 sqrt 2 = 181.019336; C^2 = 32761 against 32768
  the two-slit weight 32761 / 163840 = 181^2 / (5 x 2^15) of L2 becomes 32768 / 163840 = 1/5 exactly
  a Gram entry G_jk = C_j C_k + S_j S_k errs by at most 2 x (256 x 1/2 + 256 x 1/2 + 1/4) = 512.5 on 65536, a part in 128 (the crude bound);
  the registered totals 65448 .. 65773 on 65536 (L1, note 37 (xii)) show a part in 276 on the norm.
  a rung at W = 64 moves by at most ceil(W x 237 / 65536) = 1 (0.231)
  a rung at W = 4096 moves by at most ceil(W x 237 / 65536) = 15 (14.812)

  the host cost at N = 64: today the Gram matrix has 4096 entries (stored through N = 512, formed beyond);
  the exact form keeps 16 integers per weight and per cumulative rung, no matrix; the autocorrelation of a
  vector with s nonzero phases costs s^2 products; the sign test one P-bit inner product over N/4 terms.

  the host cost at N = 4096: today the Gram matrix has 16777216 entries (stored through N = 512, formed beyond);
  the exact form keeps 1024 integers per weight and per cumulative rung, no matrix; the autocorrelation of a
  vector with s nonzero phases costs s^2 products; the sign test one P-bit inner product over N/4 terms.

